@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1279 = private unnamed_addr constant [26 x i8] c"exception-without-exc-info", align 1
@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1280 = private unnamed_addr constant [645 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `logging.exception()` with `exc_info` set to `False`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `logging.exception()` method captures the exception automatically, but\0Aaccepts an optional `exc_info` argument to override this behavior. Setting\0A`exc_info` to `False` disables the automatic capture of the exception and\0Astack trace.\0A\0AInstead of setting `exc_info` to `False`, prefer `logging.error()`, which\0Ahas equivalent behavior to `logging.exception()` with `exc_info` set to\0A`False`, but is clearer in intent.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Alogging.exception(\22...\22, exc_info=False)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Alogging.error(\22...\22)\0A```\0A", align 1
