@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1349 = private unnamed_addr constant [1005 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for functions with `return` statements that do not have \22Returns\22\0Asections in their docstrings.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AA missing \22Returns\22 section is a sign of incomplete documentation.\0A\0AThis rule is not enforced for abstract methods or functions that only return\0A`None`. It is also ignored for \22stub functions\22: functions where the body only\0Aconsists of `pass`, `...`, `raise NotImplementedError`, or similar.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef calculate_speed(distance: float, time: float) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22Calculate speed as distance divided by time.\0A\0A    Args:\0A        distance: Distance traveled.\0A        time: Time spent traveling.\0A    \22\22\22\0A    return distance / time\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef calculate_speed(distance: float, time: float) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22Calculate speed as distance divided by time.\0A\0A    Args:\0A        distance: Distance traveled.\0A        time: Time spent traveling.\0A\0A    Returns:\0A        Speed as distance divided by time.\0A    \22\22\22\0A    return distance / time\0A```\0A", align 1
