@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1356 = private unnamed_addr constant [24 x i8] c"docstring-missing-yields", align 1
@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1357 = private unnamed_addr constant [904 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for functions with `yield` statements that do not have \22Yields\22 sections in\0Atheir docstrings.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AA missing \22Yields\22 section is a sign of incomplete documentation.\0A\0AThis rule is not enforced for abstract methods or functions that only yield `None`.\0AIt is also ignored for \22stub functions\22: functions where the body only consists\0Aof `pass`, `...`, `raise NotImplementedError`, or similar.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef count_to_n(n: int) -> int:\0A    \22\22\22Generate integers up to *n*.\0A\0A    Args:\0A        n: The number at which to stop counting.\0A    \22\22\22\0A    for i in range(1, n + 1):\0A        yield i\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef count_to_n(n: int) -> int:\0A    \22\22\22Generate integers up to *n*.\0A\0A    Args:\0A        n: The number at which to stop counting.\0A\0A    Yields:\0A        int: The number we're at in the count.\0A    \22\22\22\0A    for i in range(1, n + 1):\0A        yield i\0A```\0A", align 1
