@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1389 = private unnamed_addr constant [1209 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for under-indented docstrings.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[PEP 257] recommends that docstrings be indented to the same level as their\0Aopening quotes. Avoid under-indenting docstrings, for consistency.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef sort_list(l: list[int]) -> list[int]:\0A    \22\22\22Return a sorted copy of the list.\0A\0ASort the list in ascending order and return a copy of the result using the bubble sort\0Aalgorithm.\0A    \22\22\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef sort_list(l: list[int]) -> list[int]:\0A    \22\22\22Return a sorted copy of the list.\0A\0A    Sort the list in ascending order and return a copy of the result using the bubble\0A    sort algorithm.\0A    \22\22\22\0A```\0A\0A## Formatter compatibility\0AWe recommend against using this rule alongside the [formatter]. The\0Aformatter enforces consistent indentation, making the rule redundant.\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 257 \E2\80\93 Docstring Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/)\0A- [NumPy Style Guide](https://numpydoc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/format.html)\0A- [Google Python Style Guide - Docstrings](https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#38-comments-and-docstrings)\0A\0A[PEP 257]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/\0A[formatter]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/formatter/\0A", align 1
