@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1446 = private unnamed_addr constant [2022 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for docstring sections that are not separated by a blank line.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThis rule enforces consistency in numpy-style and Google-style docstrings,\0Aand helps ensure compatibility with documentation tooling.\0A\0AMultiline docstrings are typically composed of a summary line, followed by\0Aa blank line, followed by a series of sections, each with a section header\0Aand a section body. Sections should be separated by a single blank line.\0A\0AThis rule is enabled when using the `numpy` and `google` conventions, and\0Adisabled when using the `pep257` convention.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef calculate_speed(distance: float, time: float) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22Calculate speed as distance divided by time.\0A\0A    Parameters\0A    ----------\0A    distance : float\0A        Distance traveled.\0A    time : float\0A        Time spent traveling.\0A    Returns\0A    -------\0A    float\0A        Speed as distance divided by time.\0A    Raises\0A    ------\0A    FasterThanLightError\0A        If speed is greater than the speed of light.\0A    \22\22\22\0A    try:\0A        return distance / time\0A    except ZeroDivisionError as exc:\0A        raise FasterThanLightError from exc\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef calculate_speed(distance: float, time: float) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22Calculate speed as distance divided by time.\0A\0A    Parameters\0A    ----------\0A    distance : float\0A        Distance traveled.\0A    time : float\0A        Time spent traveling.\0A\0A    Returns\0A    -------\0A    float\0A        Speed as distance divided by time.\0A\0A    Raises\0A    ------\0A    FasterThanLightError\0A        If speed is greater than the speed of light.\0A    \22\22\22\0A    try:\0A        return distance / time\0A    except ZeroDivisionError as exc:\0A        raise FasterThanLightError from exc\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pydocstyle.convention`\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 257 \E2\80\93 Docstring Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/)\0A- [PEP 287 \E2\80\93 reStructuredText Docstring Format](https://peps.python.org/pep-0287/)\0A- [NumPy Style Guide](https://numpydoc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/format.html)\0A", align 1
