@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1491 = private unnamed_addr constant [16 x i8] c"undefined-export", align 1
@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1492 = private unnamed_addr constant [1047 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for undefined names in `__all__`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIn Python, the `__all__` variable is used to define the names that are\0Aexported when a module is imported as a wildcard (e.g.,\0A`from foo import *`). The names in `__all__` must be defined in the module,\0Abut are included as strings.\0A\0AIncluding an undefined name in `__all__` is likely to raise `NameError` at\0Aruntime, when the module is imported.\0A\0AIn [preview], this rule will flag undefined names in `__init__.py` file,\0Aeven if those names implicitly refer to other modules in the package. Users\0Athat rely on implicit exports should disable this rule in `__init__.py`\0Afiles via [`lint.per-file-ignores`].\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom foo import bar\0A\0A\0A__all__ = [\22bar\22, \22baz\22]  # undefined name `baz` in `__all__`\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom foo import bar, baz\0A\0A\0A__all__ = [\22bar\22, \22baz\22]\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `__all__`](https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/modules.html#importing-from-a-package)\0A\0A[preview]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/preview/\0A", align 1
